---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro'
import MistakeExhibits from '../../components/MistakeExhibits.astro'
import mistakes from '../../data/xla-mistakes.json'
---

<Base
  title="The mistake museum · the XLA wing · Rudrite Kernels"
  description="Real failures at the SPMD seam, reproduced and captured on eight host devices: uneven shardings, unbound mesh axes, collectives without a mesh."
>
  <div class="ws-ground">
    <section class="wband">
      <div class="wrap wgrid">
        <span class="wtag">the museum<br />xla wing</span>
        <div>
          <p class="mono-label serves">serves the xla path · three reproduced on 8 host-platform devices (jax 0.4.38, CPU), one captured on a Colab TPU v6e and labelled where it sits · fixes run and proven · <a class="wing-link" href="/mistakes">all wings</a></p>
          <h1 class="wh1">The partitioner says no, and it means something.</h1>
          <p class="wlede">
            Three exhibits come from the SPMD seam, where your sharding meets the compiler's
            rules: a spec the shape cannot satisfy, an axis the mesh does not have, and a
            collective called with no mesh in sight. All three reproduce on a laptop with eight
            fake host devices. The fourth could only come from real hardware, and it did: LAB·X2
            asks a Colab TPU for more HBM than it has, and the refusal arrives with both numbers
            attached. More of those land here as the lab gets run.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <MistakeExhibits entries={mistakes} />
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .serves { margin-bottom: 1rem; letter-spacing: 0.04em; }
  .wing-link { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: none; }
  .wing-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
</style>
